WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.365 --> 00:00:10.827
There is a building in India that has been called many things: the most perfect building in the

2
00:00:10.867 --> 00:00:14.608
world, the throne of Allah, and the jewel of India.

3
00:00:15.328 --> 00:00:20.950
This building, in the city of Agra in northern India, is the Taj Mahal, which means "Crown Palace."

4
00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:28.692
It was built to be a grand tomb for the remains of Empress Mumtaz Mahal, born Arjumand Banu

5
00:00:28.732 --> 00:00:36.013
Begum. In 1632, the empress' husband, Shah Jahan, ordered the tomb to be built as an expression of

6
00:00:36.113 --> 00:00:37.294
love for his dead wife.

7
00:00:38.495 --> 00:00:46.601
With its magnificent architecture and extraordinary beauty, the Taj Mahal has amazed visitors and pilgrims for four centuries

8
00:00:47.281 --> 00:00:50.043
and is considered to be a modern wonder of the world.

9
00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:58.286
Today, India has many religions, including Islam, Hinduism, and Buddhism, but the Taj Mahal was built in a

10
00:00:58.346 --> 00:01:01.268
time when India was primarily an Islamic country.

11
00:01:02.108 --> 00:01:07.572
From 1526 to 1858, India was ruled by the Mughal emperors.

12
00:01:08.593 --> 00:01:13.657
The Mughals were Muslims and originally came from Persia, now the country of Iran.

13
00:01:14.477 --> 00:01:17.680
They brought Persian culture, architecture, and art to India.

14
00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:23.544
The man responsible for the Taj Mahal, Shah Jahan, was born as Prince Khurram.

15
00:01:24.172 --> 00:01:27.313
He was well educated, very intelligent, and cultured.

16
00:01:28.174 --> 00:01:32.075
When he was fifteen, Prince Khurram met a young woman at the palace.

17
00:01:32.796 --> 00:01:34.956
For both, it was love at first sight.

18
00:01:35.657 --> 00:01:40.839
This Persian woman was Arjumand Banu Begum, and the couple married five years later.

19
00:01:41.759 --> 00:01:48.402
They were inseparable, and Arjumand even accompanied her husband on military campaigns across the Indian empire.

20
00:01:49.262 --> 00:01:53.344
Their extraordinary love was documented by court poets and historians.

21
00:01:54.244 --> 00:01:59.888
After Prince Khurram's father died, he took over the empire and began to use the name "Shah Jahan,"

22
00:02:00.328 --> 00:02:01.889
which means "King of the World."

23
00:02:02.609 --> 00:02:08.853
Even with her husband in this new position of power, Arjumand remained his friend, counsel, and lover.

24
00:02:09.473 --> 00:02:11.474
Together they had fourteen children.

25
00:02:12.135 --> 00:02:18.418
In 1631, when Shah Jahan and Arjumand had been married for eighteen years and he had been the

26
00:02:18.479 --> 00:02:20.800
emperor of India for three, tragedy struck.

27
00:02:21.648 --> 00:02:24.050
Arjumand was in her ninth month of pregnancy.

28
00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:29.936
Shah Jahan left the city of Agra to travel with his wife and army to Burhanpur, to put

29
00:02:29.976 --> 00:02:31.016
down a rebellion there.

30
00:02:31.777 --> 00:02:36.181
While they were away, Arjumand died while giving birth to their fourteenth child.

31
00:02:37.062 --> 00:02:38.743
Shah Jahan was devastated.

32
00:02:39.464 --> 00:02:45.369
The court historians wrote: "The king cried out with grief, like an ocean raging with storm For the

33
00:02:45.409 --> 00:02:50.878
whole week afterward, His Majesty did not appear in public From constant weeping, he was forced to use

34
00:02:50.918 --> 00:02:52.819
glasses, and his hair turned grey."

35
00:02:53.700 --> 00:03:00.765
The emperor grieved for two years, and historians recorded that he never showed enthusiasm for administering his empire

36
00:03:00.805 --> 00:03:05.708
again. Instead, Shah Jahan found solace in art and architecture.

37
00:03:06.489 --> 00:03:12.573
Six months after his wife's death, he began planning a magnificent memorial to his wife, a memorial to

38
00:03:12.633 --> 00:03:19.154
love. This memorial would consist of Arjumand's tomb, ornamental gardens, and several other buildings.

39
00:03:20.055 --> 00:03:25.759
Set on the banks of the Jamuna River near Shah Jahan's palace in Agra, the complex became the

40
00:03:25.799 --> 00:03:26.660
Taj Mahal.

41
00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:33.405
At this time, the Mughal Empire was at its peak and India was an extremely wealthy country.

42
00:03:34.165 --> 00:03:38.949
Consequently, Shah Jahan spared no expense in planning and building the Taj Mahal.

43
00:03:39.589 --> 00:03:42.992
The finest artisans and craftsmen were summoned from all over Asia.

44
00:03:43.732 --> 00:03:47.874
The chief architect was a Persian engineer and astrologer, Ustad Ahmad.

45
00:03:48.715 --> 00:03:57.800
Sculptors, designers of domes, stone carvers, calligraphers, accountants, and construction supervisors came from Persia, Syria, Turkey, and India.

46
00:03:58.681 --> 00:04:03.804
Similarly, building and ornamental materials were sourced from all corners of Asia and the Middle East.

47
00:04:04.404 --> 00:04:11.408
There was jade from China, turquoise from Tibet, and amber from Myanmarㅡover forty types of gemstones in all.

48
00:04:12.136 --> 00:04:15.699
The main building materials were white marble and red sandstone.

49
00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:24.347
Twenty thousand workers and one thousand elephants worked for twenty-three years and completed the Taj Mahal in 1653.

50
00:04:25.428 --> 00:04:31.073
Arjumand's tomb is situated almost three hundred meters from the entrance gate, at the opposite end of the

51
00:04:31.113 --> 00:04:31.973
surrounding garden.

52
00:04:32.894 --> 00:04:38.939
Four tall towers, or minarets, rise from its corners, and in the middle, there is a massive white

53
00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:44.358
dome. The tomb is made of white marble and has eight rooms inside on two floors.

54
00:04:45.198 --> 00:04:50.360
The central room is octagonal and contains the remains of Empress Arjumand and Shah Jahan.

55
00:04:51.281 --> 00:04:56.263
It was often said that the Taj Mahal was "built by Titans and finished by jewelers."

56
00:04:57.143 --> 00:05:03.066
The walls, floors, doors, and ceilings of the Taj Mahal and all its buildings are beautifully decorated.

57
00:05:03.926 --> 00:05:08.748
In one technique, gemstones are inlaid in the marble to make exquisite glittering patterns.

58
00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:14.844
In another technique, red pigment is used to create delicate floral patterns on the white walls.

59
00:05:15.724 --> 00:05:22.749
The Taj Mahal's entrance gate is richly decorated with floral patterns made from gemstones and with calligraphy in

60
00:05:22.809 --> 00:05:23.530
black marble.

61
00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:29.574
When you picture the Taj Mahal, you usually think only of the majestic, white-domed building.

62
00:05:30.354 --> 00:05:36.738
But in fact, everything around the tomb was designed to harmonize perfectly with it: the main gateway, the

63
00:05:36.778 --> 00:05:38.860
gardens, the mosque, and the rest house.

64
00:05:39.464 --> 00:05:42.467
A detached gateway is a feature of Muslim architecture.

65
00:05:43.047 --> 00:05:46.190
It is a symbol of the transition between Earth and paradise.

66
00:05:47.171 --> 00:05:49.553
A long garden runs from the gate to the tomb.

67
00:05:50.094 --> 00:05:54.738
The garden is Persian in style, with patterns based on the Islamic holy number of four.

68
00:05:55.559 --> 00:06:00.804
There are two marble canals that cross in the middle and divide the garden into four squares.

69
00:06:01.664 --> 00:06:05.408
The canals are lined with cypress trees, which symbolize death.

70
00:06:06.236 --> 00:06:11.359
Each of these smaller gardens is also sub divided by pathways into four flower beds.

71
00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:17.603
The garden was carefully designed so that there is a clear, unobstructed view of the tomb from any

72
00:06:17.683 --> 00:06:18.704
place on the grounds.

73
00:06:19.584 --> 00:06:24.567
At the center of the garden, halfway between the tomb and the gate, there is a raised marble

74
00:06:24.647 --> 00:06:26.849
tank containing water and lotus flowers.

75
00:06:27.689 --> 00:06:31.952
The tank was designed to perfectly reflect the Taj Mahal in its water.

76
00:06:33.084 --> 00:06:37.828
On either side of the tomb are red sandstone buildings; one is a mosque and the other is

77
00:06:37.868 --> 00:06:38.529
a rest house.

78
00:06:39.329 --> 00:06:43.292
Like all mosques, the mosque faces toward Mecca and is used for prayer.

79
00:06:44.213 --> 00:06:49.077
In front, a small piece of marble is polished so highly that it reflects like a mirror.

80
00:06:49.858 --> 00:06:55.102
The mosque floor sparkles with the color of red velvet and the ceiling is painted in a beautiful,

81
00:06:55.162 --> 00:06:56.063
hypnotic pattern.

82
00:06:56.823 --> 00:07:02.368
The other sandstone building is the twin of the mosque; it is identical in size and design.

83
00:07:03.284 --> 00:07:06.966
Because it faces away from Mecca, it has never been used for prayer.

84
00:07:07.847 --> 00:07:13.710
It was built as a rest house and for architectural balance, so that the tomb has two identical

85
00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:14.971
buildings on either side.

86
00:07:15.851 --> 00:07:22.175
The architects and craftsmen who worked on the Taj Mahal used some very special optical effects to enhance

87
00:07:22.215 --> 00:07:23.456
its grandeur and beauty.

88
00:07:24.216 --> 00:07:26.437
The first effect was the use of repetition.

89
00:07:26.938 --> 00:07:32.501
For example, the arch of the entrance gate is shaped like the tomb, so as you enter, you

90
00:07:32.561 --> 00:07:34.042
anticipate seeing its form.

91
00:07:34.663 --> 00:07:37.264
A second effect is due to the tomb's location.

92
00:07:37.945 --> 00:07:43.509
As you start walking toward it, it seems to grow in size, and the dome seems to slowly

93
00:07:43.609 --> 00:07:48.593
inflate. When you finally reach the base, it is colossal and magnificent.

94
00:07:49.333 --> 00:07:53.416
The other impressive effect is an optical illusion created by the calligraphers.

95
00:07:54.016 --> 00:07:58.580
Holy text from the Koran decorates many buildings, including the tomb itself.

96
00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:05.365
However, no matter how high the text is on a wall or ceiling, its size never seems to

97
00:08:05.425 --> 00:08:09.968
change! This effect was achieved by gradually increasing the height of the letters.

98
00:08:11.109 --> 00:08:15.012
Finally, the designers used nature to enhance the Taj Mahal's beauty.

99
00:08:15.833 --> 00:08:18.395
The sky is the background to the white marble building.

100
00:08:19.155 --> 00:08:25.140
Of course, this background constantly changes, and as the sky changes, the Taj Mahal changes too.

101
00:08:26.168 --> 00:08:30.030
At night, when the sky is dark, the Taj Mahal glistens in the moonlight.

102
00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:34.632
At sunset, when the sky is pink, the Taj Mahal softly glows.

103
00:08:35.592 --> 00:08:41.775
So, the Taj Mahal is captivating for many reasons: it is a monument to love, its architectural and

104
00:08:41.835 --> 00:08:48.058
artistic beauty is incomparable, and it has a spiritual quality that sets it apart from other buildings.

105
00:08:48.878 --> 00:08:53.460
When you see it you can't help wondering, does it belong to Earth or heaven?
